Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:57:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] feat: `brit ls-remote`, Git's spelling of `brit remote
 refs`

Prints Git's `<oid>\t<refname>` lines in the server's order, annotated tags followed
by their peeled `<refname>^{}` line, with Git's tail-matching patterns (`dev`,
`refs/heads/dev`, `refs/heads/feat/*`) and `--heads`, `--tags` and `--refs`. The
remote is a configured name, URL or path, or the current branch's remote. Agents
used `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/dev` to check whether the integration branch
moved; that now works in brit with the output they already parse with `cut -f1`.

